    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d439">

                <pb facs="0482" n="448" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg448"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr. von Reichenau.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-12-19"><hi rendition="#italic">December 19,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 264.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 12th instant, stating that the Government of Germany would
                    bear its share of the cost of safes for the preservation of the records of the
                    Samoan land commission and that the consular representative at Apia had been so
                    advised.</p>
                <p>Adding that a copy of your note has been sent to Mr. Churchill, the
                    consul-general of this Government there, I beg to renew to you, sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
